✔ FINDING G2-SM3R (P3, owner G1 / G5; MOCK of G2-SM2): a refresh whose user carries a NEW last_sign_in_at re-creates the open screen -- the typed text is gone at once and its record is discarded on the next look (13.732958ms)
✔ G2-SM3R-C: the same change while confirming drops the confirmation and the consent (nothing can be sent with them) (14.112292ms)
✔ G2-SM3R-S: the same change WHILE a send is out -- the new screen shows the attempt as unresolved, never as sent, and a retry re-uses the SAME id (no second post) (16.372083ms)
✔ negative controls: a route keyed by the user only brings SM3 back (text survives a new sign-in), and the old same-id condition brings G2-X1 back (a first send says "same id") (28.90975ms)
